# .spun get drop01 through gui-test.py's drop proxy, which closes the
# connection once, at the stage of the run (mame-drop.sh). drop01's install
# directory is suggested, so y at 16 s answers "Install to C:/apps/drop?".
# Every stage ends .spun with an error. ON ERROR keeps the autoexec running;
# without it the autoexec would end at the error and NextZXOS would show its
# menu. The handler prints SPUNERR with the error code and the line of .spun
# (30); the PRINT of line 40 runs only if .spun returns without an error.
# screen 39 SPUNERR 255 30 therefore means that .spun ended with an error
# before 39 s, and mame-drop.sh reads it from summary.txt. BASIC does not
# print a trapped error's message, so the screen shows .spun's own lines
# only. It has no noreset: NextZXOS fetches $0000 once when a handler catches
# the error of a dot command, with BASIC at the line of that command.
put @SPUN@ /dot/SPUN
autostart ON ERROR ERROR TO e,l:PRINT "SPUNERR ";e;" ";l:FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
autostart .spun -s @HOST@ -p @PORT@ get drop01
autostart PRINT "SPUNDROPDONE"
autostart FOR i=0 TO 1 STEP 0: NEXT i
seconds 40
key 16 y
snap 9 10 12 14 17 20 25 39
screen 39 Opening @HOST@
screen 39 SPUNERR 255 30
